{
  "info": {
    "_postman_id": "e99ec9ab-3c5d-44e7-b75d-6933224bac8d",
    "name": "TheRealCooker Backend API",
    "description": "Auto-generated from the Express codebase in backend_therealcooker.\n\nBase path mounted in server.js: `/api/v1` (see mainroute/index.js).\n\nAuth: most routes use `protect` middleware which expects `Authorization: Bearer <accessToken>`. Login/Register requests below auto-save `accessToken`/`refreshToken`/`userId` into collection variables via a test script, so once you run Login everything else just works.\n\nKNOWN ISSUES IN THE CURRENT CODEBASE (found during analysis, left untouched per request):\n1. `server.js` uses `path.join(...)` but never imports the `path` module -> server crashes on boot until fixed.\n2. `mainroute/index.js` never mounts `route/user.route.js` or `route/subscription.route.js`, so the whole 'Users' folder and 'Subscriptions' folder below are unreachable (404 via notFound handler) until someone adds `router.use(\"/users\", userRoutes)` and `router.use(\"/subscriptions\", subscriptionRoutes)`.\n3. `route/user.route.js` imports `controller/fcm.controller.js`, which does not exist in the repo -> importing that route file throws.\n4. `controller/user.controller.js` imports `Checklist`/`Report` models from `model/checklist.model.js` / `model/report.model.js`, neither of which exist -> 'Get User Details (Admin)' and 'Delete User (Admin)' will throw.\n5. `route/user.route.js` does `import upload from \"../middleware/multer.middleware.js\"` (default import) but that file only exports a named `upload` -> `upload` is `undefined`, so 'Update Profile', 'Create User (Admin)', and 'Update User (Admin)' will crash with `upload.single is not a function`.\n\nRequests affected by #2-#5 are marked '[BROKEN]' in their name/description so you know what to expect until the backend is fixed.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "auth": {
    "type": "bearer",
    "bearer": [
      { "key": "token", "value": "{{accessToken}}", "type": "string" }
    ]
  },
  "variable": [
